AltoConvexCreditLineMarket::accrueInterest()
├── when market is paused
│   └── it should revert with IsPaused for PAUSE_TYPE
├── when IRM call reverts or returns malformed data
│   └── it should propagate the failure without changing accounting
├── given an AdaptiveCurveIrm or PegResponsiveExponentialIrm
│   ├── it should accrue old-model interest before switching to the new IRM
│   ├── it should add new-model interest to active debt and claimable fees without changing credit capacity or shares
│   ├── it should exclude paused time from accrual
│   ├── it should use active debt divided by the credit limit for adaptive utilization
│   └── it should apply the peg-responsive rate after a price checkpoint
├── given the IRM call
│   ├── it should pass creditLimit as total supply assets
│   ├── it should pass current totalBorrowed assets
│   ├── it should exclude accumulated badDebtAssets from the IRM debt input
│   └── it should not query the oracle or interact with Convex or tokens
├── when returned interest is zero
│   ├── it should leave debt assets and claimableFeesAssets unchanged
│   ├── it should leave totalSupply shares and positions unchanged
│   ├── it should still call the IRM and permit it to update its timestamp
│   └── it should emit AccrueInterest with zero interest
└── when returned interest is nonzero
    ├── it should add interest to totalBorrowed assets
    ├── it should add the same interest to claimableFeesAssets
    ├── it should not change totalBorrowed shares
    ├── it should not change totalSupply assets or shares
